    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This study addresses a method to determine reservoir properties using well production histories. The focus of this report is the determination of absolute permeability values using an automated decline curve matching procedure. This procedure is used in parallel with a reservoir simulation history matching process, and practical issues relating a reservoir model and the decline curve model are addressed. An automated algorithm employing nonlinear regression to process the well history data is presented. This algorithm is then demonstrated using seven simple reservoir problems, created using the BOAST black oil simulator. These demonstrations are used to draw conclusions about the simulator well model, the decline curve procedure, and possible applications of such a method in petroleum reservoir simulation.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
